./frontend/public/brand/sidira-lockup-duo.svg:2:  <title id="title">Sidira — horizontal lockup (dual-color, standard)</title>
./frontend/public/brand/sidira-lockup-duo.svg:3:  <desc id="desc">Standard horizontal lockup: dual-color six-blade diaphragm (Sid-blue left, Avira-rose right) + SIDIRA narrow uppercase in ink. The standard mark on every surface (DESIGN.md §1.3) — in-product nav/dashboard and brand alike. The monochrome lockup (sidira-lockup.svg) is a legacy fallback.</desc>
./frontend/public/brand/sidira-mark-duo.svg:2:  <title id="title">Sidira mark — dual-color (standard, §1.3)</title>
./frontend/public/brand/sidira-mark-duo.svg:3:  <desc id="desc">Six-blade diaphragm with three Sid-blue (#2C5577) blades on the left and three Avira-rose (#D696C8) blades on the right. Geometry identical to sidira-mark.svg. The standard mark on every surface (DESIGN.md §1.3) — in-product nav/dashboard and brand alike — and the held frame inside the in-product aperture-close animation (§9.2). The monochrome mark (sidira-mark.svg) is a legacy fallback.</desc>
./frontend/public/brand/merch/sidira-sticker-mark.svg:3:  <desc id="desc">Hexagonal die-cut sticker, 38 mm point-to-point. Paper ground (#F4EFE6), monochrome ink mark (#0E1A2B). Hexagon orientation matches the mark's inner aperture: points face top and bottom, flat edges face left and right. Mark holds the §1.4 clear space (one blade-length) inside the die. The hexagon outline is the DIE-LINE: non-printing, cut path only.</desc>
./CONTEXT.md:27:`DESIGN.md` at the repo root is now the canonical source of truth for every visual, UI, and brand decision. Locked: six-blade diaphragm mark (radius-13 hexagonal aperture, vertices at angles 30/90/150/210/270/330) + narrow uppercase `SIDIRA` wordmark in Söhne Schmal (Archivo Narrow preview); ink `#0E1A2B` / paper `#F4EFE6` / signal lime `#C8FF3D` / Avira rose `#D696C8` / Sid-blue `#2C5577`; Söhne + Berkeley Mono + GT Sectra Fine type stack; 2/4/8/12/16/24/32/48/64 spacing; settle-trace + aperture-close motion bets. Color architecture encodes the founder's kids' names (Sid = ink/structure, Avira = rose/vital, lime = brand-functional) so the family meaning lives in the system without exposing pink to buyers. Replaces the legacy teal/blue split-test favicon. Codex review: 2 rounds, 1 P1 + 2 P2s, all fixed. Follow-up tickets: #135 (bake into `sidira.ai` + `app.sidira.ai`), #136 (wire dual-color aperture-close animation into result page), #137 (legacy brand-file cleanup).
./design-rethink/visions/editorial.md:193:- **How it stays tasteful (the discipline):** it is *monochrome phosphor on glass/oat*, never rainbow. It moves on **arrival** and on **commit** only — it does not idle-loop in the user's face (a barely-perceptible 0.5% brownian shimmer is the ceiling at rest). It always encodes real structure: each point is an agent, cluster centroids are persona means, convergence speed maps to agreement score. Spectacle = data. If it ever reads as decoration, it's wrong.
