./sessions/phase-5-design-system/context.md:17:- [ ] **Founder re-review of proposal R2** — `sessions/phase-5-design-system/rework-proposal-2026-06-09.md` (now Codex-amended R2); preview rebuilt at `/tmp/sidira-rework-proposal.html`. No DESIGN.md changes made yet. Founder decisions 2026-06-09: (1) fold Codex changes into proposal + preview, re-review once more, THEN DESIGN.md PR; (2) paper stays `#F4EFE6`, cooling deferred to an in-product comparison. All eight Codex changes folded in: decision-rule primitive beside the verdict (THRESHOLD 0.70 · POLICY DR-2 · "why this verdict" line), data-bound confidence trace (running-estimate series, axis-labeled), paired-difference lift viz (control→digest ticks + delta CI band), labeled seed variance, muted negative sentiment, threshold marked on CI axis, expanded provenance (run ID + readings.csv/transcripts/API links), paper reverted to spec values. Codex consult record now a section in the proposal doc (session `019eaeb6-0c81-70a0-b94f-5454727b3a70` in `.context/codex-session-id`). R2.1 polish after founder eyeballed R2 (2026-06-09): axis labels moved out of stretching SVGs into HTML overlay rows (fixes distortion), CI/lift bands thinned + opacity 0.13 so they stop reading as sliders, mitigation "GATES SHIP" on its own line, and a ▶ RUN SIMULATION live demo added to the preview (trace plots point-by-point, then §9.4 settle fires) — specced as NEW §9.7 "Live plotting" in the proposal doc. Preview then expanded to a full-product walkthrough (founder request): nav tabs now switch between five real pages — Objectives (evidence posture per goal + "now reading" glass strip), Hypotheses (list with policy-bearing verdict chips incl. DO NOT SHIP / UNDERPOWERED / QUEUED), run detail (the instrument panel), Rollouts (live-vs-sim glass comparison, frozen prediction, halt rule, an honest OUTSIDE CI miss), Calibration (reliability diagram from graded ledger, "GATED — never synthetic" tag), Library (packs/stimuli cards; draft pack ineligible for DECISIVE). Aperture iris breath while running + duo-frame commit beat also added (duo-in-nav needs DESIGN.md carve-out decision). R2.2 (2026-06-09, during founder re-review): founder asked where reverse PRDs live in the new IA — answer: the **feature pack** (already first-class in the backend, `schemas/feature_pack.py`: versioned snapshot per product, multiple capabilities each with reverse_prd + reverse_figma) was missing from the Library. Added: proposal §7 "Library IA: three entity types" (feature pack · persona packs · stimuli; reverse PRDs = PRD-document typography on paper, never glass; run provenance pins all three), preview Library page gains a "Feature pack — as-built product" section (snapshot card + 2 capability cards with REVERSE PRD links), hypothesis-detail provenance rail gains a Product row (frozen slice). **R2.3 (2026-06-10, founder request): full MVP product mock built** — `product-mock-mvp.html` (committed, same dir). Same R2 design language and 5-tab IA, but grounded in MVP truth instead of the moonshot-mature state: headline relabeled **"Simulation agreement — raw, UNCALIBRATED (ledger empty)"** per Codex Risk 2 honesty containment; chrome CAL readout shows `CAL — · n=0`; lineage rail is 4-stage with ROLLOUT/GRADED unreachable; provenance "Graded: NOT YET". Adds the two MVP-shipped surfaces the R2 preview lacked: **new-hypothesis wizard** (A/B mode toggle, persona filter chips #101, model select #103, population + Hamilton note, seeds; honest "no spinners" estimate line) and **agent chat** (arm-scoped rooms + cohort + 1:1, the differentiator; identity.md-frozen provenance, PIN TO DECISION RECORD on every message). Hypothesis detail gains a **refinement-queue section** (suggested refinements derived from register findings, QUEUE AS HYPOTHESIS → HYP-121). Moonshot tabs (Objectives/Rollouts/Calibration) render as **honest expansion slots** — dashed paper cards, "what this becomes / fed by / unlocks" spec, no synthetic data — and a board-chrome **VIEW MOONSHOT STATE toggle** swaps every slot to the future surface (R2's objectives register, live-vs-sim rollout glass, reliability diagram + grade log) so the growth path is visible in one file. Demo workspace renamed Lumen (first customer); nav gains Clerk workspace chip + avatar (Phase 5). **R2.4 (2026-06-10, founder decisions): (1) SCOPE LOCK — the real design-change PRs implement ONLY built functionality: no Objectives/Rollouts/Calibration pages; MVP nav = Hypotheses · Library; CAL chrome readout and ROLLOUT/GRADED lineage stages are future-only too (a nav that names pages that don't exist isn't an expansion slot, it's a broken promise). Mock updated to match: moonshot tabs/CAL readout carry `future-only` and appear only under the VIEW MOONSHOT STATE toggle; toggling back navigates off future pages; MVP lineage rail is just SIMULATED → DECISION; glass footer says "UNGRADED — NO LIVE OUTCOMES YET" (no dead WHY→ link). (2) WIZARD REWORK — founder flagged the new-hypothesis page as clumsy and asked if the theme is wrong; diagnosis: composition failure, not theme — the page broke the system's own rules (half-width form floating in an empty page, ALL-CAPS mono hints shouting at label volume under every field, recessed inputs heavier than the system's wells). Rebuilt in instrument posture: two-zone layout with a live "Reading manifest" inspector rail (the run card prints as you configure — Begin reading lives in the rail), numbered sections 01 Claim / 02 Subject / 03 Cohort / 04 Reading, sentence-case body-font hints, paper-elevated inputs without inset shadow. Theme itself unchanged and recommended kept; if founder still dislikes it after the rework, next step is 2–3 alternate theme boards. **R2.5 (2026-06-10, Codex theme review folded in): Codex independently confirmed keep-the-theme + same diagnosis (composition, not theme) and named the governing principle — "same system, different pressure": hypothesis detail can be severe/instrument-like, wizard feels like configuring a run, chat evidentiary but human, marketing editorial. This goes into DESIGN.md as a surface-restraint section in PR 1. Mock changes applied: (1) PRESENT mode — P key / chrome button hides the review board so the theme is judged as product, not prototype board (keydown handlers now also ignore input/textarea focus, fixing a latent bug where typing "r" in the wizard fired replay); (2) verdict lexicon containment — MVP reserves DECISIVE for the calibrated state: chips/verdict-why/CI caption read "HIGH SIM AGREEMENT · SHIP CANDIDATE / DO NOT SHIP" in MVP, "DECISIVE · …" under the moonshot toggle (Codex: honest-but-emotionally-contradictory fix); library tag mvp variant "cannot print ship candidates"; (3) chat sys-line softened to sentence-case body font (mono reserved for designators). Codex also flagged mobile as under-specified — recorded as DESIGN.md PR-1 requirement: mobile = "stacked instrument readout", not a squeezed desktop panel. Paper #F4EFE6 stays (already decided; Codex concurs it's the memory bet).** **R2.6 (2026-06-10, founder question "where and how can I create new stimuli?"):** answer is two-layered. In the BUILT product there is no standalone stimulus entity — grep confirms "stimulus" appears nowhere in the backend; the stimulus is carried inline on the hypothesis (`schemas/simulation.py` `Hypothesis.prose` + optional `proposed_prd` + `proposed_figma`), control arm is implicitly the as-built feature-pack slice, so creation today = filling those fields in the new-simulation flow (no reuse, no versioning). In the mock IA the two designed entry points are the wizard's "+ new stimulus…" select option and Library → Stimuli, but the Stimuli section lacked a creation affordance (persona packs had the Builder ghost card; stimuli had nothing). Fixed: added a "New stimulus" ghost card to Library → Stimuli with mvp/future split — MVP variant is honest ("AUTHORED IN WIZARD", Today row "lives inside the hypothesis — wizard 02 · Subject", link routes to the wizard); moonshot variant shows the future first-class entity (versioned, reusable across hypotheses). Card states the invariant for both: control = as-built slice, never authored; you author only the treatment (prose + proposed PRD + screens). Implication recorded: promoting stimulus to a first-class Library entity is a future backend migration (extract Hypothesis's three fields into a versioned record); MVP implementation keeps stimuli inline per the R2.4 scope lock. Follow-up (founder: "so clicking on new stimulus opens a form?"): the wizard's "+ new stimulus…" option is now WIRED in the mock — selecting it discloses an inline authoring panel inside 02 · Subject (dashed-border well: name + type FLOW/EMAIL/PAGE, "Treatment — proposed change" textarea = proposed_prd, optional "+ attach screens" = proposed_figma, and the invariant line "CONTROL ARM = AS-BUILT CAPABILITY FROM THE FROZEN SLICE — NEVER AUTHORED"); the manifest rail Stimulus row live-updates to "sample-workspace-v2 · NEW · 2 ARMS". Deliberately inline disclosure, NOT a modal or navigation to Library: matches the backend reality (the fields live on the hypothesis), keeps the wizard's configuring-a-run pressure, and means the MVP implementation needs zero new backend (the panel just populates Hypothesis.proposed_prd/proposed_figma). The Library ghost card remains the future managed path. **R2.7 (2026-06-10, founder approved ticket plan): implementation tickets FILED — #156 is now the tracking epic** (checklist comment issuecomment-4667926801). 7 implementation PRs + 1 backlog: #163 PR1 DESIGN.md+lib/design.ts (gates all; needs R2 sign-off + 4 open decisions: duo-in-nav, favicon §1.3, fonts, DO-NOT-SHIP wording), #164 PR2 token sweep + TopNav shell (labels Hypotheses · Library, routes unchanged), #165 PR3 hypotheses register /simulations, #166 PR4 instrument panel /simulations/[id] (highest value), #167 PR5 wizard recompose + inline stimulus authoring /simulations/new (recompose only — proposed_prd/figma already in built wizard + api-types.ts, zero backend), #168 PR6 Library /personas (feature pack + persona packs + stimuli derived view), #170 PR7 agent chat evidentiary restyle /agents/[id] (was missing from first table — caught and added), #169 backlog: stimulus as first-class backend entity (out of R2 scope). Dependency order: #163 → #164 → (#165–#168, #170 parallel). All filed as ram-de, assigned ram-de. **R2.8 (2026-06-10, founder mock review): two fixes.** (1) Library stimuli "AUTHOR IN WIZARD →" was landing on a blank wizard — now deep-links (`data-author-stim`): wizard opens with "+ new stimulus…" preselected, authoring panel disclosed and scrolled into view. (2) Founder asked why there's no window to create a feature pack — answer: correct by design, feature packs are GENERATED by sidira-crawler (R2 versioned snapshots, atomic `latest` pointer per `adapters/feature_pack_loader.py`), never hand-authored; the as-built pack IS the control arm, so editing it would corrupt every reading. The Library now says so: "New snapshot" ghost card in the feature-pack section (chip GENERATED — NEVER AUTHORED; mvp: PROVISIONED AT ONBOARDING — RE-CRAWL IS AN OPS ACTION + "WHY NO EDITOR? — IT'S THE CONTROL ARM"; future: weekly Playwright cadence + REQUEST RE-CRAWL →). Both specced onto #168 (issuecomment-4667965246; deep-link interplay noted for #167). **R2.9 (2026-06-10, founder follow-up): (1) "where is the window to START the crawl?" — real ticket-map hole found.** Crawl today is operator CLI only (`sidira-crawler run --customer <id> --snapshot <ver>`); no API, no UI; walker itself still open (sidira-crawler #1–#3, Phase 7, blocked by first customer). Persona packs got the full builder window set (#22–#28) but feature packs never got the equivalent — **filed #171** "[Phase 7] feature pack builder — crawl setup + trigger window" (setup: capabilities + entry URLs + role logins; trigger endpoint wrapping run_crawl via worker like persona-builds #24; walk progress per capability; diff + promote gate; Library RE-CRAWL routes here; invariant: configures the crawler, never edits pack content). Mock's feature-pack ghost card future state now shows Setup row + "CRAWL SETUP + RE-CRAWL →". (2) Stimuli "author in wizard" passing through the hypothesis form is BY DESIGN in MVP (a stimulus only exists as fields on a Hypothesis — a standalone window is exactly #169); relabeled the MVP link "AUTHOR INSIDE A NEW HYPOTHESIS →" to set expectations. If that handoff grates as a user, that's the signal to pull #169 forward — founder's call, flagged. **R2.10 (2026-06-10, founder: "where is the #171 window in the mock?"):** built it — new `page-crawler` ("Feature pack — crawl setup", future surface, reached only via the moonshot-state ghost-card link "CRAWL SETUP + RE-CRAWL →"; toggling moonshot off while on it navigates back to Library). Same two-zone instrument posture as the wizard: evidence form 01 Capabilities (chips, 5–10) / 02 Entry points (1–3 URLs per capability) / 03 Access (sandbox tenant + per-role test users + IP allowlist hint, "walker never touches production") / 04 Run (cadence weekly/on-demand, walk depth 3 hops); inspector rail = "Crawl manifest" (customer, snapshot DRAFT, counts, roles, depth, diff target, Promote GATED — REVIEW DIFF FIRST, latest FLIPS ON PROMOTE) with Start crawl → / Save setup and est line "WALKED CAPABILITIES PRINT AS THE CRAWLER LANDS THEM. NO SPINNERS." Page header tag carries the invariant: GENERATED — NEVER AUTHORED · THE PACK IS THE CONTROL ARM. This is the design reference for #171 (Phase 7 implementation, not part of the R2 rollout PRs). **R2.11 (2026-06-10, FOUNDER SCOPE CORRECTION): "crawler UI and the crawler changes are not moonshot and they are part of the MVP."** This amends the R2.4 scope lock for this one surface and overrides the R2.9/R2.10 Phase 7 framing. Executed: (1) MOCK — `page-crawler` is now an MVP surface: the feature-pack ghost card's mvp/future split collapsed (dropped "PROVISIONED AT ONBOARDING — RE-CRAWL IS AN OPS ACTION" and the "WHY NO EDITOR?" dead link; Setup + Cadence rows and the "CRAWL SETUP + RE-CRAWL →" link now visible in both states), the snapshot card Source row reads "PLAYWRIGHT CRAWL · 2026-06-01" in both states (was "MANUAL SNAPSHOT · AUTO-CRAWL PENDING" in MVP), and the modeToggle guard that bounced page-crawler back to Library on moonshot-off is removed. The GENERATED — NEVER AUTHORED invariant is unchanged everywhere. (2) TICKETS — #171 retitled "[MVP] frontend+backend: feature pack builder — crawl setup + trigger window", body rewritten (scope-correction note; design-reference section pointing at page-crawler; dependencies: frontend window on #163→#164, parallel with #165–#168/#170; trigger/progress backend on sidira-crawler #1–#3; setup form + saved config can land before the walker). sidira-crawler #1–#3 retitled [Phase 7]→[MVP] (rationale comment on crawler #1: founder declared crawler work MVP, no longer blocked-on-first-customer framing). Epic #156 comment (issuecomment-4668074228) amended to MVP. Net: MVP ticket set is now #163–#168, #170 (R2 restyle PRs) + #171 (new functionality, alongside) + sidira-crawler #1–#3; #169 remains the only backlog/future item from this rework. **R2.12 (2026-06-10, founder resolved all four #163 open decisions** — recorded on #163, issuecomment-4668268668; body checklist struck through): (1) duo commit-beat in nav APPROVED with carve-out — §1.3 gains "decision-commit beat" as an Animated trigger, nav prohibition clarified to resting color only; (2) favicon stays duo-on-paper as shipped (`app/icon.svg` unchanged) — §11's stale "paper mark on ink" line and CLAUDE.md's "never for the favicon" wording get fixed in PR 1; (3) fonts: ship the §3 fallback stack (Hanken Grotesk / Archivo Narrow / JetBrains Mono / Instrument Serif) as MVP production, zero purchases, swap to Söhne/Berkeley Mono/GT Sectra at marketing push (founder overrode the buy-Berkeley-Mono-only suggestion); (4) verdict lexicon: HIGH SIM AGREEMENT single stem both polarities (· SHIP CANDIDATE / · DO NOT SHIP), CLEAR SIM SIGNAL rejected, DECISIVE still calibrated-only. #163 now has no open questions — the remaining gate is founder sign-off of R2 itself. Also this window: `acceptEdits` set as `permissions.defaultMode` in `.claude/settings.json` (uncommitted — shared file, founder to decide if it rides a PR or moves to settings.local.json). **R2.13 (2026-06-10, "R2 is signed off, start PR 1"): PR 1 (#163) IMPLEMENTED** in worktree `design-r2-pr1` (branch `worktree-design-r2-pr1`). DESIGN.md rewritten to v0.2 — section numbering preserved for external references (§10 refuse list, §9.x): Grid folded into §7.3, NEW §7.4 surface restraint / §7.5 mobile / §7.6 Library IA, §8 repurposed as Data furniture (decision-rule primitive, verdict lexicon table MVP vs calibrated, honest numbers, charts, sentiment, pending states, provenance grid), §9.4–9.7 motion specs added, refuse list extended (glass beyond live readings, decorative marks, verdict-without-policy, spinners/skeletons, calibrated-UI-before-backend, count-up numerals), §11 icon.svg line fixed, §12 changelog 0.2 entry. All four R2.12 decisions folded in. NOTE: fallback family is **Archivo** per signed-off R2 (supersedes the Hanken Grotesk wording in R2.12 item 3; GT Sectra dropped entirely so no serif fallback either — FONT_SERIF marked @deprecated in lib/design.ts, removed in #164 with its two consumers app/page.tsx + app/about/page.tsx). lib/design.ts: rule → rgba(14,26,43,0.16), added glass/glassRule/glassText/glassMuted/success (gitnexus impact TOKENS: LOW, 0 upstream). CLAUDE.md favicon wording reconciled. Codex review GATE PASS (0 P1, 3 P2 — all fixed: §9.1+§9.3 reduced-motion end states added, §7 nav claim framed as target-spec landing in #164, duo SVG <desc> metadata updated to §1.3 brand-mode list). gitnexus detect-changes: LOW, 0 affected processes. Frontend typecheck + build pass. (`npx gitnexus analyze` side-effect churn in AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md gitnexus blocks reverted — not part of PR 1.) **MERGED 2026-06-10: PR #172, squash commit `2b571bf`, #163 auto-closed, worktree removed.** **R2.14 (2026-06-10, "ok, start 164"): PR 2 (#164) IMPLEMENTED — PR #174 open** from worktree `design-r2-pr2` (branch `worktree-design-r2-pr2`, code commit `6a0e752`, 12 files +160/−111). Global token sweep onto `lib/design.ts` TOKENS (no globals.css/Tailwind exists — sweep is entirely on inline styles): greens `#0a7d3a`→success, reds `#a30000`→alert, ambers→warn ACCENT-ONLY, invented blue `#1d4ed8`→ink, tinted bgs→paperRecessed, grays→rule/inkMuted, purple staging badge→inkMuted-on-paperRecessed (§10); CI bands as token hex-alpha (`${TOKENS.ink}40` 25%, `${TOKENS.warn}59` 35%) so tokens stay the single source. §8.5 applied: sentiment chips all sit on paperRecessed with rule borders, only positive keeps color (success), negatives inkMuted — glyphs +/~/− carry the signal. §4.3 applied: PM/agent/collective/synthesis designators are ink-weight (ink vs inkMuted), never color. "running" status = ink (live = §9.5 lime carrier only, never lime/blue text). Motion: `EASE_MECH`/`EASE_SETTLE` exported per §9.3; TopNav uses 80ms ease-out color + 160ms EASE_MECH underline. TopNav rebuilt per mock: 56px bar on paper, 1px rule, tabs **Hypotheses · Library** (labels only, routes unchanged, Product dropped), 13px/500, 2px ink underline, aria-current; R2.4 scope lock honored (no future-only tabs/CAL/⌘K). Clerk chrome: organizationSwitcherTrigger as workspace chip (mono 11px, rule border, radius 2), userButtonAvatarBox 26×26 r2. Fonts §5.1 fallback-as-production: Archivo replaces Hanken Grotesk as --font-sans, Instrument Serif dropped entirely, FONT_SERIF deleted + both consumers migrated to Archivo Narrow SemiBold uppercase heroes (clamp sizing, lh 1.1, ls 0.01em). Verification grep over app/components/lib: zero legacy hexes, zero serif refs. GATES: gitnexus impact — **ThumbsControl HIGH** (callers AgentChatPage/CollectiveTurn/SynthesisTurn, 4 flows; mitigation: colors-only, flag/onSet contract untouched), all else LOW; detect-changes 12 files/31 symbols/15 flows HIGH on breadth but all expected presentational symbols; tsc+build ✅; codex review 0 P1, **P2 real catch: `TOKENS.warn` #D9A300 as text ≈2.0:1 on paper, fails WCAG large-text 3:1 → warn is accent-only forever (bands/markers/borders), mid-range 60–79 score text + "CI crosses zero" caption → inkMuted** (fixed, re-gated green; rule encoded as code comments at use sites), P3 (don't commit `.claude/skills/gitnexus/`) already excluded; `gitnexus analyze` AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md churn reverted pre-commit. Awaiting founder review/merge of #174.
