./sessions/phase-5-design-system/context.md:138:The mark proves the brand thesis ("this is an instrument") with iconic camera-iris geometry that has heritage in JPL/Hubble/Leica/oscilloscope reticles. The narrow uppercase wordmark is the only typographic register in the Linear/Vercel/Statsig peer lineup that doesn't sit in the "Y Combinator lowercase sans" template — it gives Sidira authority instead of approachability. The animation moment (aperture closing, dual-color appearing) enacts the design thesis literally: ink at rest, color when the instrument is reading evidence. The dual-color carries Sid + Avira meaning, scoped to two specific surfaces (in-motion + founder-mode), so the family-name story lives without ever appearing on a buyer-facing dashboard. Lime signal-accent stays the brand-functional color for live state — instrument-correct, oscilloscope-phosphor-coded, escape velocity from the cyan/violet lane every peer occupies.
