    62	and app-icon use case (the duo-color mark on a paper-filled rounded-square
    63	ground, `viewBox 0 0 144 144`). Its stroke is fixed at `3.5` in viewBox units —
    64	calibrated to read across the 32 → 144 px size range that Next.js generates
    65	icons at. Browsers downscaling to 16 px will produce a thinner stroke; this is
    66	acceptable for the favicon trade-off. Do not import `icon.svg` as a reusable
    67	mark; use `sidira-mark.svg` with the stroke override above.
    68	
    69	### 1.3 Color states
    70	
    71	The mark has two sanctioned color states. Anything else is wrong.
    72	
    73	| State | When it appears | Color |
    74	| --- | --- | --- |
    75	| **Static default (dual-color)** | everywhere — product nav · dashboard · in-app UI · favicon · app icon · public site (`sidira.ai`) · `/about` · press kit · social avatar · business card · screenshots · all surfaces not mid-animation | dual-color (3 Sid-blue blades + 3 Avira-rose blades), static |
    76	| **Animated (transient)** | inside the product while a simulation is being computed, while a confidence trace is settling, during persona-group fan-out, and the **decision-commit beat** (one non-looping aperture cycle when a verdict commits — §9.2) | cycles dual-color → through the aperture-close animation → dual-color (§9) |
    77	
    78	The dual-color lockup is **the standard mark on every surface, in-product
    79	nav and dashboard included.** There is no monochrome-vs-dual split and no
    80	brand-surfaces-only reservation: the mark rests dual-color everywhere — the
    81	product nav, the dashboard, the console shell, and buyer-facing product UI all
    82	carry the Sid-blue + Avira-rose split at rest. The mark may still *pass
    83	through* the aperture-close animation during the transient states above (the
    84	§9.2 keyframes still apply during a simulation run and the decision-commit
    85	beat); the animation note remains valid. `ink` monochrome is no longer a
    86	mark color state — it is reserved for the wordmark and structure (§2).
    87	
    88	**RATIONALE (founder, 2026-06-26, ticket #35):** the founder chose visual
    89	brand consistency over the brand-vs-product split. One mark, one color story,
    90	on every surface a user or buyer ever sees — the dual-color aperture is the
    91	identity, not a special-occasion variant. This deliberately overrides the
    92	prior "monotone in-product / dual-color brand-surfaces-only / never resting
    93	in the nav or dashboard" policy.
    94	*(Two-state consolidation + everywhere-standard dual-color: founder decision,
    95	2026-06-26.)*
    96	
    97	### 1.4 Clear space
    98	
    99	Clear space minimum equals **one blade-length** (= mark width / 4) on every
   100	side. In horizontal lockups, the wordmark sits inside this clear space — it is
   101	the only thing allowed there.
   102	
   103	### 1.5 Mark assets
   104	
   105	| File | Use |
   106	| --- | --- |
   107	| `frontend/public/brand/sidira-mark-duo.svg` | **standard mark** — dual-color (Sid-blue + Avira-rose), used everywhere (§1.3) |
   108	| `frontend/public/brand/sidira-mark.svg` | legacy monochrome mark, `currentColor` stroke — fallback only, no longer default (§1.3) |
   109	| `frontend/app/icon.svg` | favicon / app-icon (duo-color mark on paper ground, `rx: 32`) |
   110	
   111	---
   112	
   113	## 2. The wordmark
   114	
   115	**`SIDIRA`** — narrow uppercase, no glyph trickery, no dots, no embellishments.
   116	
   117	| Property | Production target | MVP / fallback (shipping now) |
   118	| --- | --- | --- |
   119	| Typeface | **Söhne Schmal Halbfett** (Klim Type Foundry) | Archivo Narrow SemiBold (free, Google Fonts) |
   120	| Weight | 600 | 600 |
   121	| Case | uppercase always | uppercase always |
   122	| Tracking | `+60` (= `letter-spacing: 0.06em`) at 24 px and above | same |
   123	| Tracking (small) | `+80` (= `letter-spacing: 0.08em`) at ≤ 16 px | same |
   124	| Color | `ink` (`#0E1A2B`) default · `paper` on dark surfaces | same |
   125	
   126	The wordmark is never lowercase, never italic, never given a dot embellishment,
   127	never paired with a tagline inside the lockup. The lockup is mark + `SIDIRA` —
   128	nothing else.
   129	
   130	---
    45	## Worktree Rule
    46	
    47	All PR and feature branch work MUST be done through an isolated worktree.
    48	
    49	### Always Do
    50	
    51	- **MUST call `EnterWorktree` before starting any branch or PR work.** Never edit code on a named branch in the main checkout — always get a fresh worktree first.
    52	- After the PR is merged (or abandoned), call `ExitWorktree` to clean up.
    53	- Session file commits (`/pythia-session save`) are the one kind of commit that may land on a feature branch: a **worktree session** commits its session file directly to the feature branch, where it rides the PR and lands on `main` at merge. Only a **main-checkout session** (rare) uses the branch-hop dance to commit directly on `main`.
    54	
    55	### Never Do
    56	
    57	- NEVER make code edits on a feature branch in the main checkout.
    58	- NEVER commit code changes (non-session) directly to `main`.
    59	
    60	### Why
    61	
    62	Worktrees give each PR an isolated filesystem, preventing stale state, accidental cross-contamination between branches, and the "wrong branch" class of errors. The `bgIsolation: worktree` setting in `.claude/settings.json` enforces this for background agents automatically; the rule above extends it to foreground sessions.
    63	
    64	## Backend Deploys Are Manual
    65	
    66	api.sidira.ai does NOT auto-deploy; only the Amplify frontend rebuilds on push
    67	to `main`. **After any merge to `main` that touches `backend/`, prompt the user
    68	to redeploy the backend** — otherwise the live app 404s on the new routes while
    69	prod silently serves the previous build. Include this in the merge wrap-up:
    70	
    71	```
    72	~/.npm-global/bin/codex exec "Read deploy/REDEPLOY.md in this repo and execute the backend redeploy for api.sidira.ai. If a step needs the AWS console, walk me through it."
    73	```
    74	
    75	`deploy/REDEPLOY.md` is the agent-executable runbook (staleness check,
    76	`SIDIRA_AUTO_MIGRATE` decision for Alembic migrations, SSM deploy command,
    77	verification). If the merged PR added a migration, say so explicitly in the
    78	reminder — that changes the runbook's step 2.
    79	
    80	## Design System
    81	
    82	`DESIGN.md` at the repo root is the canonical source of truth for every
    83	visual, UI, and brand decision. Read it before:
    84	
    85	- Adding or editing any UI component.
    86	- Touching colors, typography, spacing, radius, or motion in CSS / Tailwind.
    87	- Creating a new SVG, image, or marketing surface.
    88	- Building a new page or screen.
    89	- Reviewing a PR that touches `frontend/` for visual correctness.
    90	

